{"id":"theocracy","name":"Theocracy","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:theocracy"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Theocracy","text":"A word first used by Josephus to denote that the Jews were under the direct government of God himself. The nation was in all things subject to the will of their invisible King. All the people were the servants of Jehovah, who ruled over their public and private affairs, communicating to them his will through the medium of the prophets. They were the subjects of a heavenly, not of an earthly, king. They were Jehovah’s own subjects, ruled directly by him (comp. 1 Sam. 8:6-9)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6963","lemma":"קוֹל","xlit":"qôwl","gloss":"a voice or sound","kjv":"aloud, bleating, crackling, cry","count":6,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H3988","lemma":"מָאַס","xlit":"mâʼaç","gloss":"to spurn","kjv":"abhor, cast away, contemn, despise","count":2,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H3190","lemma":"יָטַב","xlit":"yâṭab","gloss":"to be make well, literally or figuratively","kjv":"be accepted, amend, use aright, benefit","count":2,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H8050","lemma":"שְׁמוּאֵל","xlit":"Shᵉmûwʼêl","gloss":"Shemuel, the name of three Israelites","kjv":"Samuel, Shemuel","count":2,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H3162","lemma":"יַחַד","xlit":"yachad","gloss":"a unit","kjv":"alike, at all, both, likewise","count":2,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H7626","lemma":"שֵׁבֶט","xlit":"shêbeṭ","gloss":"a scion","kjv":"correction, dart, rod, sceptre","count":2,"share":0.11}],"verses":["Exod.24.3","Deut.5.25","Deut.5.26","Deut.5.28","1Sam.8.7","1Sam.8.19","Exod.19.8","Exod.24.7","Deut.5.27","Deut.5.29","Deut.33.2","Deut.33.3","Deut.33.4","Deut.33.5","Judg.8.23","1Sam.10.19","1Sam.12.12","2Chr.13.8"],"related":[{"id":"government","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"sinai","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.038,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"instability","type":"cooccur","shar